== 3. The thermal routes, bounded
3a LO-01a: the thresholds (MODELED, PS-SURV-R at PLAN heat, +40 C; on shore the front end's and charger's loss on the loads adds 1.725 W; the block's lowest film).
   The conductance from which each criterion holds (W/K), the same in either lid state:
   cell rating (+60 C)                                            on the pack  1.2455
   the +59 C abort (FEA-008 LO-01a)                               on the pack  1.3154
   H1 not acting (reading under +56.5 C, no sensor allowance)     on the pack  1.5300
   H1 not acting with the 0.71 K reading-high term                on the pack  1.6043
   SGP41 inside air at most +55 C                                 on the pack  1.5630
   F2 at the inside air at most +60 C                             on the pack  1.1723
   cell rating (+60 C)                                            on the shore 1.2498
   the +59 C abort (FEA-008 LO-01a)                               on the shore 1.3156
   H1 not acting (reading under +56.5 C, no sensor allowance)     on the shore 1.5149
   H1 not acting with the 0.71 K reading-high term                on the shore 1.5831
   SGP41 inside air at most +55 C                                 on the shore 1.6664
   F2 at the inside air at most +60 C                             on the shore 1.2498
   The cell rating alone: 1.2455 W/K on the pack. FEA-008's own LO-01a criterion (the +59 C abort): 1.3154 W/K. The complete E3-A and E3-L pass line: 1.6664 W/K (SGP41 inside air at most +55 C, on shore).
   T-H1 must read at least 1.666 W/K with the fans, lid closed AND lid open (the heat stage runs in both). The record's bounds: independent 1.06 to 2.49 (closed) and 1.22 to 2.85 W/K (open);
   appendix 32.53 1.5 to 2.0 (closed) and 3.0 to 3.3 W/K (open). Lid open at the bound's lowest 1.22 W/K the cells on the pack reach 60.39 C and the air on shore 60.49 C: past +60 C as well.
   Dependencies that fail today and stay visible: On board B as generated the stage criteria fail at any level where the heat stage is entered, because its one-module stage lacks the LoRa mesh and APRS (TEST-PLAN E3-L); F2's body (P13, PWR-F12); the gauge's ADC and gradient terms (P14, not in the thresholds above); HIGH heat (not covered).
3b The pocket coupling measure: the block's east face (0.00509 m2) against the east wall through a gap filler of the pocket's widest gap (9.68 mm, CASE-MARGINS M4b; k 1.0 W/mK, ASSUMPTION),
   its base (0.00756 m2) on the floor through the heater mat (1.5 mm, k 0.2 W/mK, ASSUMPTION; the mat's sheet states neither: True); the other four faces (0.01697 m2) in the inside air at 5.0 to 15.0 W/m2K.
   Coupling to ambient 0.0544 (worst) to 0.0901 W/K (best), to the inside air 0.2545 (worst) to 0.0848 W/K (best): f = 0.824 to 0.485; the enclosure loses 0.0377 to 0.0735 W/K of skin (counted); a 3 W/mK filler adds 0.0015 W/K.
   LO-01a lid closed at the bound's lowest: cells 63.29 C without it (two-node reproduces pwr_budget: True), 58.64 C (worst) to 51.99 C (best) with it; on shore 59.30 C. Against the complete pass line:
      cell rating    58.64 C against 60.00 C: holds
      the +59 C abort 58.64 C against 59.00 C: holds
      H1 reading     58.64 C against 56.50 C: fails by 2.14 K
      SGP41 air      61.94 C against 55.00 C: fails by 6.94 K
      F2 at the air  61.94 C against 60.00 C: fails by 1.94 K
   So the measure closes the cell criteria only; the air criteria are the enclosure's (3a). It is a fallback for the cells, never a substitute for T-H1's conductance.
   Placement: the block's top lies about 3.66 mm under board B's underside (SHORTLIST's 2.66 mm of room plus the 1.0 mm minimum, CASE-MARGINS M6), which has no local model (POWER-THERMAL.md 9.2).
3c The cold end the measure touches (LO-01b; PS-IDLE-SPEC on the pack, lid open, -20 C, the highest conductance): cells -5.52 C without it, -10.24 C with it (-9.22 C on W4's highest);
   holding -8.0 C (1 K over UTD's -9.0 C reading, INFERRED) takes 0.38 W into the cells, 0.44 W from the battery with the mat's regulator (1.0 % of PS-IDLE-SPEC's 42.82 W; firmware owner).
3d Charging at the cold end: the mat puts 7.5 W into the block (MAKER, RS PRO 245-556 at 12 V) and its regulator 1.0 W into the air (POWER-THERMAL.md 7.1); at -20 C on input power, the pack idle,
   the cells reach 12.44 C (record's model) and 12.84 C (with the coupling): over UTC's 1.0 C and the panel's +3 C hold (MODELED).
3e Storage hold times (INFERRED): the cells' own time constant in the pocket 1081 to 4457 s; the closed, stopped kit 1.53 to 3.97 h (32.53's 8 to 10 kJ/K over the lid-closed still-air bound).
   After 24 h from the most favourable start (steps of 91 K and 78 K) the cells lag the ambient by 0.21 K (hot) and 0.18 K (cold) as one node, 0.351 K and 0.301 K as two nodes
   (the kit's 9340 J/K beside the cells' 660 J/K, 0.70 W/K to ambient, 0.1481 W/K to the cells). Heating the whole kit at the -20 C floor for 24 h would take 218 to 452 Wh (the first issue's figure);
   heating only the pack is 3g.
3f LO-01f passive: to keep the cells within 80 K of the start for 24 h against a 91 K step (two nodes, the slowest kit), the pack's coupling must fall under 0.0207 W/K from 0.1481:
   24.6 mm of insulation at k 0.02 W/mK (ASSUMPTION) round the block, against 0.77 to 2.66 mm of room in D-06's pocket: REJECTED within the pocket (today the cells move 90.65 K).
3f LO-01g passive: to keep the cells within 65 K of the start for 24 h against a 78 K step (two nodes, the slowest kit), the pack's coupling must fall under 0.0173 W/K from 0.1481:
   30.3 mm of insulation at k 0.02 W/mK (ASSUMPTION) round the block, against 0.77 to 2.66 mm of room in D-06's pocket: REJECTED within the pocket (today the cells move 77.70 K).
3g LO-01g, the -33 C storage margin (E4-S, 24 h), in three cases. Ambient and cell temperatures are kept apart; the pack's discharge window (-10 to +60 C, 3.12) governs
   whenever the pack feeds a heater, the storage rows only when it does not. One boundary: the source's terminals; the mat's 7.5 W into the block, its regulator's 0.133 of that into the air,
   the gauge's NORMAL draw (336 uA typical, MAKER SLUSC67B 6.5: 0.0048 W) when the pack feeds it. Slow and fast corners: 0.1222 and 0.3400 W/K in series (pack, air, case).
   WITHDRAWN as a feasibility basis: the comparison of 38.1 to 106.1 Wh with the pack's nominal 144.7 Wh. It is a nominal comparison; the usable-energy comparison below replaces it.
   (i) A warm pack kept inside its limits for the exposure.
      Fed by the pack: the heater discharges the cells, so the setpoint is UTD's -9.0 C reading plus the published cold-side budget 0.86 K = -8.14 C (the gradient and ADC terms TBD).
      Hold: 2.97 to 8.20 W into the cells, 3.37 to 9.30 W at the pack's terminals, 80.9 to 223.1 Wh for 24 h with no cool-down credit.
      Usable at the stored charge: 30 % (Ver. 1.1 3.13) less the 5 % reserve, aged to 80 % (SC-23), times the cold factor at the setpoint, unknown between MAKER 7.5's 0.41 (1C, -10 C) and 1.0:
      11.9 to 28.9 Wh, so the heat lasts 1.3 to 8.6 h of the 24 h, a reserve of -211.2 to -51.9 Wh after the exposure; from a full charge 4.9 to 32.6 h.
      And in the stored state the gauge is in shutdown: 'In SHUTDOWN mode, the device turns off the FETs after FET Off Time' (MAKER, SLUUAQ3A 5.4.2), so the pack-fed heater has no protected path unless the gauge stays awake.
      Scope: not available at REQ-025's stored state (its shutdown and its 30 % charge); with the gauge awake and a full charge, 4.9 to 32.6 h, so 24 h only at the low-demand, high-cold-factor end.
      Fed by a separate primary source (the pack stays in its storage row and in shutdown): setpoint the -20 C floor plus the thermostat's tolerance and the in-pack gradient (both TBD):
      1.59 to 4.42 W into the cells at the floor itself, 38.1 to 106.1 Wh for 24 h driven direct (42.2 to 116.6 Wh through the 12 V regulator), plus 2.93 to 8.16 Wh per K of margin.
      Start and control: a thermostat on the block, independent of the gauge and the kit (both off), arms with the stored state and closes at its setpoint; the source must deliver at -33 C.
      Its usable energy at -33 C, the thermostat's tolerance, the gradient, a place in the case and its transport classification (D-04) are NAMED UNKNOWNS: its duration is not computed.
      Cool-down credit (ASSUMPTION: E4-S's starting state is not stated; from the sheet's 23 C standard temperature): 1.57 to 4.57 h before the pack reaches -8.14 C, 2.58 to 7.27 h before -20 C.
      Recovery: E4-O follows E4-S (4 h at -20 C); a pack held at the -20 C floor is below the -10 C discharge floor, so E4-O starts from shore or vehicle input or after
      warming, as TEST-PLAN and D-02d already allow; a pack held at -8.14 C could start from itself.
   (ii) A pack already cold-soaked before any heater starts: below -20 C it has already left its storage row and no heater undoes that; between -20 and -10 C the pack may not
      discharge (3.12) and the gauge holds its discharge FET off below UTD (recovery -4.0 C), so only a separate source can rewarm it: 0.133 to 0.183 Wh into the cells per K, plus the losses.
      Its scope if the unknowns land: E4-S's 24 h at -33 C from a warm stored kit, the source supplying at least 38.1 to 106.1 Wh at -33 C plus 2.93 to 8.16 Wh per K of margin and its own reserve.
      F2 sits at about the inside air (-30.7 to -30.0 C at the hold), below its -20 C operating floor: Eaton's answer, or the heated zone extended to board P (a Layer 7 item).
   (iii) Heating lost, or its energy spent, at the pack-fed hold: the cells pass the -20 C floor 0.30 to 1.09 h later (two nodes, from the heated steady state); a separately fed
      hold at the floor itself passes it at once, so its margin must cover the source's depletion as well. Neither the gauge (in shutdown) nor the kit records the event (a named item).
3h E5's cycle: TEST-PLAN states 10 cycles of 24 h between 30 and 60 C and no dwell or ramp. Any passive network passes the cycle's mean, so the pack's surroundings average
   the mean ambient plus the rise: storage can help only if the mean ambient is under 40.78 C (worst rise) to 53.37 C (best). For a symmetric cycle (mean 45 C, 15 K amplitude, ASSUMPTION):
   possible at the worst corner: no; at the best a 5.68 h time constant, regeneration in the cool half included, so 14.4 to 21.2 mm of insulation or 3.0 to 9.1 kJ/K of added heat capacity,
   against 0.77 to 2.66 mm and a full pocket: INCONCLUSIVE until the profile is stated; for the symmetric profile, not within D-06's pocket.
3i Powered cooling (a thermoelectric stage; COP 0.5 to 1.0 ASSUMPTION; hot side at most 30 K over the ambient it rejects to):
   E3-O  hold 56.50 C: cold-side load 0.76 to 7.87 W; through a path out of the case it needs 0.051 to 0.525 W/K (COP 1.0) or 0.076 to 0.787 W/K (COP 0.5); into the inside air the loop closes at the worst corner: COP 0.5 no, COP 1.0 yes
   E5    hold 56.50 C: cold-side load 1.50 to 10.09 W; through a path out of the case it needs 0.100 to 0.673 W/K (COP 1.0) or 0.150 to 1.009 W/K (COP 0.5); into the inside air the loop closes at the worst corner: COP 0.5 no, COP 1.0 yes
   E3-S  hold 57.93 C: cold-side load 1.60 to 4.44 W; through a path out of the case it needs 0.106 to 0.296 W/K (COP 1.0) or 0.160 to 0.444 W/K (COP 0.5); into the inside air the loop closes at the worst corner: COP 0.5 no, COP 1.0 yes
   The pack's own skin path (3b) is 0.054 to 0.090 W/K: enough only at E3-O's best corner. E3-S has no input: 38 to 213 Wh over 24 h from a separate source.
   INCONCLUSIVE, the inputs missing: a cooler's maker sheet, the input's spare power (L4-E4's 4.70 A limit less the kit's load, not derived here), the volume, a sealed path out of the case.
3j PWR-F12's key-down: 18 A for 60 s (6.0 A a cell) from C1's +55 C warms the cells 1.37 to 3.24 K adiabatically (MODELED), to 56.37 to 58.24 C, inside +60 C.
3k P13's hour at 10 A (3.33 A a cell): the cells' own 4.67 to 8.00 W, a steady rise of 10.5 to 54.0 K over the block's film and 25.5 to 60.0 K adiabatic over the hour (MODELED):
   'the block at the pack's hot limit' holds the cells inside +60 C only if the limit is set at the cell surface and the chamber runs that much cooler (a definition item for P13's owner).
3l E3-L's levels at the bound's lowest lid-closed conductance (MODELED): +20 C: the reduced mode, air 49.90 C, cells 52.04 C; +30 C: the heat stage (C1 acted), air 52.12 C, cells 53.29 C; +40 C: the heat stage (C1 acted), air 62.12 C, cells 63.29 C

