   min 2.80 Ah, 121.0 Wh nominal; 10 A continuous; cut-off 2.75 V; charge to 4.2 V; USD 3.50 (a marketplace seller, not the maker; 10 to 4,999 pieces). Its figures are INFERRED (a page, not a specification).
Read and set aside: LG INR18650HG2 (MAKER, LG Chem INR18650HG2 product specification BCY-PS-HG2-Rev0 (13 October 2014), v2/vendor/battery/held/lg-inr18650hg2-rev0-2014.pdf): discharge -20 to 75 C in 2.9 but -20 to 60 C in its own 5.1 cautions, storage 1 month -20 to 60 C, 1 year -20 to 20 C
   (its own text limits it to +60 C, and the one-year row fails LO-01h); Molicel INR-18650-P28A (MAKER, E-One Moli Energy MOLICEL INR-18650-P28A product data sheet, v2/vendor/battery/molicel-inr18650-p28a-v1.pdf): ambient charge 0 to 60 C, discharge -40 to 60 C, no storage clause (True), min 2.60 Ah.
Energy at the kit's conditions (MODELED, pwr_budget.usable at PS-IDLE-SPEC 42.82 W, +20 C, aged to 80 %, the 35E's rate table for all three, INFERRED for S2 and S3):
