   route INCONCLUSIVE: a heater fed by a separate primary source, keeping a warm pack at the storage floor (case i; the CANDIDATE). 38.1 to 106.1 Wh into the cells for the 24 h at the floor itself, driven direct, plus 2.93 to 8.16 Wh per K of margin; a cold-soaked pack (case ii) is not recovered, and a lost heater (case iii) is past the floor at once. Missing: the source's usable energy at -33 C, the thermostat's tolerance, the in-pack gradient, a place in the case, its transport classification (D-04)
   route INCONCLUSIVE: a cell whose maker's sheet covers the level, with the protection and control redesign as its entry cost (section 4). the HL18650V's page stores from -40 C; the 2015 30Q sheet stops at -30 C. Missing: a maker's signed specification covering the level (none held; the HL18650V's page is not one), F2's replacement, U2 and the hot-stop thresholds re-derived
   gap: a primary source's usable energy at -33 C (at least 3g's demand plus margin and reserve), the thermostat's tolerance, the in-pack gradient, a place in the case, its transport classification, F2 at about -30 C (Eaton). Next: read one lithium primary maker's sheet at -33 C and size it against 3g
LO-01h CONDITIONAL (evidence MAKER)
   acceptance, complete: the bought lot's sheet covers -20 C for three months and +25 C for a year (BAT-F09); E4-T at the governing floor
   route CONDITIONAL: procurement. Ver. 1.1 covers both rows. Missing: the lot's revision
   gap: the purchase record
Closable now: none. No collision: LO-01b, LO-01c. Conditional: LO-01a (T-H1 at least 1.666 W/K in each lid state, and its failing dependencies), LO-01h (the lot's revision).
Open engineering obligations: LO-01d, LO-01e, LO-01f, LO-01g, each with at least one route INCONCLUSIVE on named inputs (above); none has every route rejected.
SELECTION: A1 (4b), the 35E as ruled with local thermal management; no cell change and no spend now. S2 is not recommended (it moves no margin row on its own sheet, misses LO-01h's year at its 23 C and costs 11.9 % of the energy).
OWNER DECISION: none is forced (rows with every route rejected: none). A1 changes no approved constraint; A2, A3 and a pack-fed heater would (D-06's cell or pocket, REQ-025's
   stored state), and none of them is needed while A1's routes stand; A1's purchases are the owner's spend only when made. A missing cell rating is a component limitation plus
   missing feasibility evidence, not a contradiction between owner requirements (D-29, D-36, cell_provenance). FEA-008 stays open as the session's engineering obligation.
Possible later changes (none proposed now; each would be the owner's only once every route of a row within the requirements is shown unavailable on bounded evidence):
   A. (a requirement change) the four margin levels shown with the pack out of the exposure, as REQ-074 and REQ-051's deviations already run them: no spend, no energy lost;
      the kit not claimed at those levels with its own pack. Reserved to the owner by D-29; not proposed, because routes remain open.
   B. (a resource change) a wide-temperature 18650 inside D-06's 4S3P: its maker's signed specification (the request is drafted), the protection and control redesign (section 4),
      about USD 42.00 a pack of 12 cells, 121.0 Wh nominal against 144.7 (16.4 % less usable), D-06's 'about 145 Wh' restated: spend and D-06 need the owner's approval (cell_provenance).
   C. (the existing state) FEA-008 open as the session's engineering obligation, a release gate on those rows; no ruling is needed for it.

== 6. The battery path's other thermal items (PWR-F12, F2 and the protection temperatures)
F2 (MAKER, Eaton SCF9550 ELX1135 (effective January 2022), v2/vendor/battery/eaton-scf9550-elx1135.pdf): operating -20 to +60 C; 'Storage temperature: -10 °C to +40 °C < 90% RH'; endurance lines '+105 °C @ 1000 hours' and '-40 °C @ 500 hours' (test conditions, not a rating).
   Board P sits beside the block, so F2 is at about the inside air or the cells (INFERRED): past its operating range at LO-01a's worst corner True (62.12 C), LO-01d True, LO-01e True, LO-01f True,
   LO-01g True; its storage line, if it covers a mounted part, also misses the storage envelope (cold True, hot True): Eaton (clarification/eaton-scf9550.txt, extending Q-E2).
   F2's own 0.32 to 0.81 W at 18 A is unpublished in rise, so its margin after a key-down from +55 C stays PWR-F12's (P13). The coupling changes neither the key-down nor F2's air.
U2 (BQ7720700): its fixed 70 C over-temperature trips somewhere in 62.7 to 77.5 C at the network, so at the +71 C storage margin a destructive trip of a fitted pack is permitted (True), not certain.
The gauge's thresholds stay inside REQ-046's windows (OTC 44.0, OTD 57.5, UTC 1.0, UTD -9.0 C; THERMAL-COORDINATION.md section 5): this record moves none. With the coupling the block
   gains a gradient (wall side cooler, the side under board B hotter), so the thermistors go on the hottest cells and P14's gradient term is re-measured (INFERRED).

